       "text": "I haven't entered this order. You've confirmed the dose, but you haven't given a clinical reason for it. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I can't find a situation in a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function where it would be safe. Because the drug has a long half-life, an overdose can't be quickly reversed.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily right now. If the patient needs more blood pressure control, the dose can be titrated, or a second agent can be added.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or the attending.** If you think a supratherapeutic dose is warranted, a pharmacist or attending physician can review it. The order can then be entered with their documented approval.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** The order may have come from a note or handoff where \"5 mg\" was misread as \"50 mg.\"\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it."
